6-
7-## At a glance
8-
9:Horizon is Minecraft: Java Edition 26.3 rewritten from scratch in Rust, so it runs faster on the same computer. Single player, LAN, servers, resource packs and Horizon's own mods work today, on your own copy of the game.
10-
11-**Being done now**
12-
13-- **Steady frames at long render distances**: Making Horizon faster than vanilla on every computer, with smooth camera movement even at 32 chunks, by spreading the work better over the processor's cores.
14:- **Modpacks' world generation, natively**: Making the world-generation mods of popular modpacks (new structures, YUNG's dungeons and mineshafts, packs built on Lithostitched) generate their worlds in Horizon, natively and fast.
15-- **Single player as a server: the last differences**: Single player now runs a small server in the background, as vanilla does. We are fixing what still behaves differently there; every fix also works for LAN and server players.
16-- **Vanilla parity: the player-visible gaps, closed**: Every method of the Java game is tracked with where Horizon does it, and the differences players can see are being closed, list by list: mobs, blocks, items, screens, rendering, servers.
17:- **Mods**: Mods for Horizon, as one line of work led by the modding team: native mods the launcher builds into your game, mods on servers, mod screens and settings, tools for mod makers, the registry and machines.
18-
19:**Next**: Fresh benchmarks against vanilla; Faster world creation and entry on small CPUs; Low-end computers: Steam Deck, old Macs, 8 GB; Native upscaling; Server console, bans and a full admin API; Hosting polish: Windows service, safe updates; One single-player path: remove the in-frame world; Faster block lookups; Playing on servers: everything shows as it should; Shader packs, written again from scratch; A new launcher design; Splitscreen.
20-
21-**How to help**: Play it and tell us what differs from vanilla (Discord or GitHub), run the benchmark on your computer, vote for what you want next, or pick one of the Help wanted items.
22-
