55:### Modpacks
56-
57:#### Modpacks' world generation, natively
58-
59:Making the world-generation mods of popular modpacks (new structures, YUNG's dungeons and mineshafts, packs built on Lithostitched) generate their worlds in Horizon, natively and fast.
60-
61:Owner: [ThatCakeIsAPie](https://github.com/ThatCakeIsAPie) · Tracking: [#3913](https://github.com/horizon-rust/horizon/issues/3913)
62-
63-<details><summary>Technical</summary>
64-
65:`horizon-port-pack` carries a pack's data-driven content over, and 26.2 data packs are upgraded to 26.3's format ([#3369](https://github.com/horizon-rust/horizon/issues/3369)). In review: worlds taller than 32 sections and each level's shape from its dimension type ([#3480](https://github.com/horizon-rust/horizon/issues/3480), [#3488](https://github.com/horizon-rust/horizon/issues/3488)), data-pack biomes in local and remote worlds ([#3491](https://github.com/horizon-rust/horizon/issues/3491)), block state providers ([#3802](https://github.com/horizon-rust/horizon/issues/3802)), surface rules by biome id ([#3366](https://github.com/horizon-rust/horizon/issues/3366)), Lithostitched's pool and processor modifiers ([#1777](https://github.com/horizon-rust/horizon/issues/1777)). Mods whose Java code does more than world generation don't run ([docs/modpacks.md](docs/modpacks.md)).
66-
67-</details>
