69:### Mods and API
70-
71:#### Mods
72-
73:Mods for Horizon, as one line of work led by the modding team: native mods the launcher builds into your game, mods on servers, mod screens and settings, tools for mod makers, the registry and machines.
74-
75-Owner: [levzzz5154](https://github.com/levzzz5154) · Tracking: [#3911](https://github.com/horizon-rust/horizon/issues/3911)
76-
77-<details><summary>Technical</summary>
78-
79:One item for all modding work ([#3911](https://github.com/horizon-rust/horizon/issues/3911)), led by levzzz5154; the order between the parts is theirs. Native mods on stable hook points (game/native_hooks.rs, [#3345](https://github.com/horizon-rust/horizon/issues/3345), [#3346](https://github.com/horizon-rust/horizon/issues/3346), [#3434](https://github.com/horizon-rust/horizon/issues/3434), [#3435](https://github.com/horizon-rust/horizon/issues/3435)) built by the launcher ([#3388](https://github.com/horizon-rust/horizon/issues/3388), [#3855](https://github.com/horizon-rust/horizon/issues/3855)); server-side hooks ([#3878](https://github.com/horizon-rust/horizon/issues/3878), [#3706](https://github.com/horizon-rust/horizon/issues/3706)); mod-owned screens, input and drawing; tools for mod makers (templates, `native.py check`); the registry ([#1634](https://github.com/horizon-rust/horizon/issues/1634), [#1642](https://github.com/horizon-rust/horizon/issues/1642), [#1659](https://github.com/horizon-rust/horizon/issues/1659)); machines with inventories and menus ([#1189](https://github.com/horizon-rust/horizon/issues/1189)); mods that read and change the world through the server. [docs/native-mods.md](docs/native-mods.md).
