5592:## Trait mods (draft)
5593-
5594-`cargo horizon-mod new <path> --template native --horizon <commit>` writes a trait mod to start from: the bundle's
5595-`horizon-mixin.toml`, pinned to that Horizon commit, and an `[api]` crate whose `hooks()` greets each player who
5596-joins. Its files are what a bundle may carry ([api/mod-files.md](api/mod-files.md)), so the launcher builds the folder
5597-as it is (`native-build <path>`) and packs it into a `.hnmod`.
5598-
5599-A bundle declares its trait mod package by its path inside the bundle:
5600-
5601-```toml
5602-[api]
5603-path = "engine"
5604-```
5605-
5606-The package may use only crates and versions in Horizon's `Cargo.lock`, like mixin crates.
5607-The folder contains a Rust package with a `horizon-client` dependency. Its library exports
5608-`pub fn hooks() -> Box<dyn horizon_client::mod_api::Hooks>`. The launcher links this package
5609-into a generated game executable and calls `hooks()` in dependency order (a mod after the mods it
5610-depends on, else in bundle order). The package is not a
5611-`[[crate]]`: it depends on the game instead of the game depending on it. A bundle with no
5612-injections, state, bridges, modules, mixin crates or post-build steps skips horizon-mixins.
5613-
5614-The package may depend on the bundle's own `[[crate]]`s by path, a sibling folder of the package in the bundle
5615-(`shared = { path = "../shared" }` from `engine/`, where `shared` is a `[[crate]]` with `path = "shared"`). The
5616-launcher points that dependency at the crate's staged copy, `native-crates/<mod>/<crate>`, so the crate is built once
5617-with the game, as a `[[crate]]`'s own is. Any other path is refused, since only the package's folder is copied.
5618-A crate used this way follows the same rules as a `[[crate]]`: no `horizon-client`, and only crates in Horizon's
5619-`Cargo.lock`.
5620-
5621-Turning a trait mod off in Options > Mods takes effect at once: the game skips its `Hooks` from the next dispatch on,
5622-on the server thread and in the window alike, and turning it on again resumes it, with no rebuild while it is still in
5623-the build. It stays loaded and keeps what it holds; what it registered at start (blocks, items, component types)
5624-stays registered, and its `RenderHooks` keep drawing until a restart. Mixin code is not switched: it checks
5625-`native_on` itself, as before ([design/mod-hotload.md](design/mod-hotload.md)).
5626-
5627-### Dependencies between trait mods
5628-
5629-A mod can publish functions and statics from its `[api]` package for another mod to call:
5630-
5631-```toml
5632-[dependencies]
5633-base_mod = "^1"
5634-extra_mod = { version = "^2", optional = true }
5635-```
5636-
5637-Requirements use Cargo semver syntax and are checked against each installed bundle's `[mod] version`,
5638-not its Cargo package version. The dependent and every installed dependency need an `[api]` package.
5639-Missing required dependencies, incompatible versions and cycles stop the build with the mods named.
5640-An absent optional dependency is permitted; an installed optional dependency must match its requirement.
5641-
