2:# Automatic game releases (docs/release-flow.md). Horizon ships only the Nightly since 2026-10-28 (Ludovic): this
5:# settle goes out without another merge) and by hand, tools/release_train.py decides, for a commit whose checks and
8:# once for a pull request labelled release-now. RELEASES_PAUSED=1 (repository variable) stops it; so does an open issue
9:# labelled release-blocker, forced runs too (nightly-build.yml checks again before publishing). One Nightly build at a
10:# time, at most 12 a day (release-now and force=true pass the cap). No `vX.Y.Z` game release is made any more.
11:#   gh workflow run release --ref <branch>                       # dry run: decides, starts nothing
12:#   gh workflow run release -f dry_run=false -f force=true       # on main: a Nightly now, whatever the rules say
15:  workflow_dispatch:
16:    inputs:
27:  # The open release-blocker issues (decide).
32:  # One release at a time. A hand-started dry run publishes nothing, so it can't race a real release: it gets a
33:  # group of its own. In the shared group, a release queued behind it replaced it as the pending run and GitHub
34:  # cancelled it (#2779's dry run, 2026-10-27), which happens all day while releases go out in batches.
