## Objective
- Implement GitHub issue #6 on `promikailamin/horizon_modloader`: make Horizon load native mods at runtime (Fabric/Forge-like, no game compile on player side), patch the `promikailamin/horizon` fork, and create a release on that fork's repo.

## Important Details
- Workspace: `/home/runner/work/horizon_modloader/horizon_modloader`; fork clone for edits: `/tmp/horizon-work/horizon` (created via `git clone --filter=blob:none --no-checkout`, sparse-checkout limited to `crates/horizon-client*`, `crates/horizon-mod-api-gen`, `crates/horizon-mods`, `crates/horizon-hooks`, `docs`, `launcher/src`, `.github/workflows`).
- `gh` is authenticated as `promikailamin` with broad scopes; fork `promikailamin/horizon` exists (default branch `main`, parent `horizon-rust/horizon`, ~525 MB, no releases). Modloader repo release `hmloader-v0.1.0` exists.
- Existing project `hmloader` implements `.hmmod` format 1 (`kind: "prebuilt-game"`): deterministic ZIP, `hmmod.json` manifest, SHA-256 per file, bundles prebuilt `horizon-client`; CLI commands `info/install/list/remove/verify/launch/convert/pack/import-launcher/doctor`.
- Prior issues #4/#5 concluded runtime loading needs an upstream ABI; that conclusion must be revised now that the fork adds one.
- Horizon trait mods: `crates/horizon-client/src/mod_api.rs` has `pub type Mods = Arc<[Box<dyn Hooks>]>`, `static MODS: OnceLock<Mods>`, `pub fn mods()`, `pub fn name_mods(ids: &'static [&'static str])`, `static MOD_IDS: OnceLock<&'static [&'static str]>`, `static OFF: OnceLock<Box<[AtomicBool]>>`.
- `crates/horizon-client/src/entry.rs`: `main()` calls `main_with(Default::default())`; `main_with(mods: Mods)` sets `MODS` first.
- `crates/horizon-client/src/main.rs` calls `horizon_client::entry::main()` with static `MOD_API_LEVEL: [u8; 27] = horizon_mods::api_level::MARK`.
- `crates/horizon-client/src/lib.rs` and `src/client_lib.rs` both have `#![forbid(unsafe_code)]` — so unsafe loader code must live in a separate crate; only safe calls allowed from `horizon-client`.
- `crates/horizon-client/src/game/native_hooks.rs` has `pub(crate) const NATIVE_HOOKS_API: u32 = 645;`.
- `libloading` 0.8.9 already in `Cargo.lock`; workspace edition 2024, rust-version 1.95.
- `crates/horizon-client-render/src/logging.rs` exports `pub fn game_home() -> PathBuf`.
- Launcher generates a trait-mod executable via `launcher/src/native_mods/api.rs`; generated main calls `name_mods` then `entry::main_with`.
- Trait mod template: `crates/cargo-horizon-mod/template/native/{api.toml,lib.rs,horizon-mixin.toml}`; manifest uses `[mod] id/version`, `[api] path = "api"`, dependency `horizon-client = { git = ..., rev }`.
- ABI safety decision: strict checks on runtime mod: exact `ABI_VERSION`, exact `RUNTIME_API_LEVEL` (from `NATIVE_HOOKS_API`), exact `TARGET`, exact rustc `--version` string, and exact Horizon revision when both sides know it.
- Design: mod `cdylib` exports `horizon_runtime_mod_v1() -> *mut DescriptorV1`; descriptor holds `hooks = *mut c_void` pointing at leaked `Box<Box<dyn Hooks>>`; host does `*Box::from_raw(hooks as *mut Box<T>)`, and `std::mem::forget(library)` so vtable/code stay mapped.
- To combine compiled + runtime mods without changing `Mods = Arc<[...]>`, plan is new `entry::main_with_owned(Vec<Box<dyn Hooks>>)` / `main_with_named(Vec<...>, Vec<&'static str>)`, and patch launcher generated main to use it; official `entry::main()` switches to `main_with_owned(Vec::new())`.
- Modloader plan: add `kind: "runtime-mod"` support in manifest; `pack-runtime`/`build-runtime` commands; `launch` accepts `--host` or `HORIZON_RUNTIME_HOST`, sets `HORIZON_RUNTIME_MODS` (path-separated) and launches runtime-enabled host; documentation `docs/RUNTIME_MODS.md`, README updates, tests.
- Git workflow requirement: incremental commits/pushes to `main`; final `git status`, `git add -A`, `git commit`, `git push`; comment on issue #6 with changes/tests/commits; never claim untested success.

